---
description: >-
  Spec #1368, #1432. The markdownAlwaysOn twin of label-syntax-shape-data.mmd: the same source
  with the setting on, so every label is markdown. The plain node draws bold and italic and the
  code-span node draws inline code; the markdown string, the tags and the written backslash-n
  draw as in label-syntax-shape-data.mmd. The picture differs from that fixture.
config:
  markdownAlwaysOn: true
---
swimlane-beta LR
  subgraph L1 [written]
    A@{ label: "plain **bold** _ital_" }
    B@{ label: "`markdown string **bold** _ital_`" }
    C@{ label: "code span a `code` b" }
  end
  subgraph L2 [formatting]
    D@{ label: "tags <b>bold</b> <i>ital</i><br>next H<sub>2</sub>O" }
    E@{ label: 'written one\ntwo' }
  end
  A --> B --> C --> D --> E
